========================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================

**N/A** (no product macros). No source change this turn. 7.x not rewritten.

Nothing in Path A **expands** user code before the SECRET sink scan.
Therefore a macro-body second pass has **no surface** and cannot be an
FN-hide. Live product host:

- **No expand walker:** `macro_expand` / `ast_macro` appear in `oodac/*.oo`
  **only** in `check_residual.oo` L28–29 (name-eq refuse). Zero
  `expand_macro` / `token_paste` / `concat_idents` / `HASHHASH` helpers.
- **`#[]`:** lexer has **no** `#` token (`token_scan_punct.oo` returns
  empty → `Unexpected character '#'`) — `#[Secret]`, `#define`, `#include`
  all **lex-fail** on check / tokens / emit-c / emit-llvm.
- **Token-paste `##`:** same `#` lex-fail. `$tok` lex-fails on `$`.
- **`macro` is IDENT**, not `KW_*` (`keyword_kind`). `macro leak(x) {…}`
  → `ERR\tparse\tunexpected IDENT`. Not a form.
- **EBNF / GBNF / tree-sitter:** no `macro` / `#[]` / attribute / paste.
- **String `"${tok}"`:** one `STRING` token; emit `oo_str_lit("${tok}")`
  — **not** interp (5.8 residual, not 2.8 expand).
- **Control:** `// SECRET: tok` + `println(tok)` still dual-path
  `ERR\tsecret` (check + emit-c + emit-llvm).
- **7.x:** not rewritten.

Domain A (when landed) owns refuse-until-later + `s28_macro_secret_smoke`.
This file owns **expansion-hide**: `#[]` / `##` / invented paste.

