========================================================================
WHY EXPAND WOULD MATTER (attack class)
========================================================================

`check_secret_println_sinks` walks **source** `toks` after `tokenize_lines`
(`c_emit.oo:86`, `check_drive.oo:62`, `llvm_emit.oo:79`). If a macro
rewrote `HIDE!(tok)` → `println(tok)` **after** that walk, the sink IDENT
would be invisible. Path A has **no** such rewrite, so the attack class
is **vacuous**.

